                                "id": "reading-task-1",
                                "title": "Passage 1 - Urban Ecology",
                                "stimulus": {
                                    "text_html": "<article><h2>Urban Bird Ecology<\/h2><p>Cities create unique ecological niches that influence the behavior and distribution of bird species. Researchers have documented shifts in feeding strategies, nesting sites, and vocalizations as birds adapt to urban noise and architecture.<\/p><p>While some species thrive in human-altered habitats, others decline due to habitat fragmentation and reduced food diversity. Understanding these dynamics helps urban planners integrate biodiversity considerations into city design.<\/p><p>Long-term studies reveal that microclimates, artificial light at night, and seasonal food availability shape population dynamics in subtle but measurable ways.<\/p><\/article>"
                                },
