                                "id": "reading-task-2",
                                "title": "Passage 2 - History of Technology",
                                "stimulus": {
                                    "text_html": "<article><h2>The Printing Press and Knowledge Networks<\/h2><p>The introduction of movable type accelerated the circulation of ideas across Europe, reshaping scholarly communities and commercial markets. Printers acted as editors, entrepreneurs, and cultural intermediaries.<\/p><p>Standardization of texts reduced copying errors but also introduced new gatekeeping roles that influenced which works reached broad audiences. The economics of production affected genres, formats, and the geography of book trade.<\/p><p>These changes fostered feedback loops between technological capability and social demand, laying foundations for modern knowledge networks.<\/p><\/article>"
